  {
    "episode_id": 86127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "say before we just jump into some of our questions is I respect the fact that Senator Baldwin responded to comments that I made in several forms that we're about to have this national convention in our backyard. And as Black Americans, as Black Madisonians, we're not feeling included. This is a party that, by and large, we have voted for. Growing up, we heard older Black uncles and aunts, and grandma's talking about what the Democratic Party has done for us. And I've stressed this also with Ben Wickler. I've said to others because I want to be a part of the solution. And I've just said I'm feeling a sense of abandonment. I'm hearing people talk about being disillusioned and not motivated. And so I'm hoping that this conversation will go somewhere and will either Encourage your colleagues, you and your colleagues to think differently about this or to put together different strategies, but to know that that's there because there's time to turn this tide. Whether it's perception or not, there's time to address it. because Wisconsin is a major state in this upcoming election, a major swing state. And we cannot afford to have unmotivated black people at home. And so the senator's office reached out to me. I didn't reach out to them. I just made those statements and just said, I'm the most tender, clergy person in this city, irrespective of race and background. I'm a part of almost every major black political, social, fraternal organization, church organization, And none of us are talking about our connections with our key representation. And so this is an opportunity to give you a platform senator to respond to some of the things that I'm hearing. Black voters say and white voters who care about how blacks feel in this election. So with all of that being said, I'm very sincere when I say I respect you and your time and your willingness to be here and talk to you today.",
