    "turn_text": "that in the meantime, I'm not out there saying, please vote for me in six years, please vote for me in five years, please vote for me in four years. Hopefully I'm out there listening and saying, this is what I'm working on and I want your, you know, how would this impact you or how, and let's work together on it. which is a very different interaction with communities and individuals in the state than it is when I am saying I'm on the ballot in five months and I want you to register to vote. This is how you do it and I want you to vote for me. So I really think that The importance is to sort of judge at least individual candidates on when you're not on the ballot, what's the level of interaction? And how are you involving your constituents in making the change that they want to see as well as things that I'm working on. So we haven't talked about my motivations for getting involved in politics, but it was all about health care and all about my being a child with a serious childhood illness and being uninsured because then after I got well, I was a kid with a pre-existing health condition and I went without health insurance and I thought that was wrong and I worried about how much my grandparents worried about an illness or an injury being catastrophic in our family and that became my fight that brought me into public service. Well, That's a fight that many people are still fighting today. And it's really important for me to hear people's stories to figure out how we get it right and how we get it",
