    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 122,
    "turn_text": "Yes. Senator, I know you thank you. I know you have a very busy schedule. You have another meeting to get into and you're so gracious to meet with me and talk with me today. I hope the conversation continues. Any information that your office would like to share about some of those initiatives that benefit black folks, I'd love to share with our listeners and constituents because it's not just, the concern is not just seeing candidates at election time, but it's what they're doing in terms of policy Because again, we have this reputation in the state of Wisconsin. We just have this sense that elected officials can help us. So it's not a criticism as much as it's a plea for help that's turning into a criticism. Because I want to see black people come to the polls. I want to see great change. And I don't want to miss this moment. So I hope that some of what we talked about will help you provide some motivation of sharing it with colleagues. so that because there's still time to talk, even using Zoom to reach out to key leaders who can influence people to really get to the polls, because we cannot afford for black people to not vote in this election. We have enough structural things with gerrymandering, and we saw what happened with Jill Koroski's, to have the pressures of what the Republicans are doing, and the lack of a clearly articulated vision for my democratic friends. We can't have the convergence of that because that will keep Black people in their homes. And back at hand, Trump was constant again. And neither you nor I want that. So if we can, Senator, let's continue talking. I appreciate your time. I want you to get to your next meeting. Thank you for the work that you do for us. And Black people want to feel like we have great representation, that we have access when we want to see change, we want to believe. We're here because we believe in Wisconsin, but we need to believe that Wisconsin believes in us. So please help us create that reality, Senator. And",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Black people should come to the polls.",
        "confidence": 0.96
